WEBVTT

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:12.930
He's alive?

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.390
What? You all look
like you've seen a ghost.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.100
No, we're just glad you're safe.

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:22.140
You know, it will take more than that
to kill me.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:27.860
I defeated those bugs and found
the key to getting out of here.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.730
That's how I made it back in one piece.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.700
INSECTS AWAKEN

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:08.960
Don't worry, I'm fine.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:11.380
I'm so sorry! It's my fault!

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:14.000
Find your own food, at the very least!

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:21.390
From the looks of it...

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:24.060
I doubt this is safe to eat.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.640
It doesn't look like
the poisonous mushrooms in this book.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.270
I'm willing to try it.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.150
Ms. Iwashimizu got it for us, after all.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:34.860
Fine, but only try a little.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:35.900
Sure.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.030
I'm really sorry!

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:40.360
I knew the risks, Ms. Iwashimizu.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.820
You don't have to apologize.

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:44.490
But Mr. Aota, you...

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:47.250
You can call me Arashi.
Everybody else does.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:49.000
Oh, okay.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:53.340
It's a good thing Ms. Botan insisted
I only try a little. She saved me.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:58.340
Although, I get the feeling
that she's hiding something.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:02:59.260
What?

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:04.260
Part of it is because she's more prepared
for survival than any of us.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:08.100
It's almost as if she knew
we would end up in this situation.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.810
Well, nothing is clear right now,
but there's one thing we're sure of.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:14.770
What?

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:17.070
That mushroom is bad news.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.740
We'll check things one at a time.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:23.740
Looks like it's morning already.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.870
Yes.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.540
She must be worried.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:28.330
Your mother?

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.120
No, my girlfriend.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.460
She must be worried sick about me.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:35.460
She's probably upset and crying.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.800
That's why I've got to get back.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:49.350
I thought I had killed him, but now...

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.770
I wonder if we can trust him.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:56.940
Well, we know he's not lying
about escaping from those bugs alive.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.070
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:09.450
Wait, isn't this the waterfall
where you got injured?

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:11.500
Hey, what are you up to?

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:18.420
Those bugs are going to come for us.
What are we doing here?

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:20.460
The bugs won't come.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:21.470
Why?

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:24.800
Shut up and follow me a little further.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.640
POISONOUS MUSHROOM

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:31.560
What? You're already okay?

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:33.140
I'm feeling much better.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:34.230
What's that?

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:37.940
Well, I'm taking notes
so we don't make the same mistakes.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:42.280
Let's give it a name.
The "Gutpunchshroom"!

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:46.360
Or maybe "Barfshroom" or "Pukeshroom."

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:47.870
The "Spewshroom"?

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:48.780
That's perfect!

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.330
You've got a talent for this,
Ms. Iwashimizu!

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:55.250
Glad to see you back on your feet.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:56.710
Thanks for looking after me.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:02.880
There should be more food
if we're going to survive.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:06.300
There should be more.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:10.640
How long does Semimaru plan
on staying in bed?

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:12.810
-Semimaru! It's time to get up!
-Hey...

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:14.680
-I heard Ms. Botan say,
-We have a lot to do!

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:17.560
-"There should be more of us."
-I have low blood pressure.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.480
-More of us?
-Yes.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.110
What is that supposed to mean?

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:24.190
-Are there other people here?
-Everyone is waiting.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.030
-I don't know.
-I'll be there in a second.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:29.910
It must mean that Ms. Botan knew
we would end up here.

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:32.490
Or at the very least,
she isn't telling us everything.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.410
-Ms. Iwashimizu, go grab your things.
-What?

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:36.750
Let's make a break for it.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:40.340
It's possible that she's a member
of the group that kidnapped us.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.510
-I'll drag you out by force if I have to.
-Ms. Botan.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:45.420
-I'm going to get more bananas.
-Okay. Go ahead.

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:46.630
-Enough, Semimaru!
-Let's go.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:48.090
-Okay.
-Cut it out, Big Sis!

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:53.180
First, we'll need to find
more food and water.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.270
Then, we can think of a way
to get off this island.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:57.350
Right.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:00.360
You really want to go back, don't you?

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:01.360
What?

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:06.150
I mean, earlier, you said
that you're worried about your girlfriend.

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.110
I did.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.610
What kind of person is she?

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:09.860
What do you mean?

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:12.870
She must be really beautiful.

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:17.500
I would love to show you a picture,
but I don't have my wallet or cell phone.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:19.790
Anyway, I think she's pretty.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:22.540
How about you? Do you have a boyfriend?

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:24.920
What? No, not at all.

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:28.680
There's no one on Earth
who would be interested in me.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:29.970
What makes you say that?

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:31.890
You seem pretty cute to me.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:35.140
I bet there are lots of guys
who secretly have a crush on you.

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:36.930
There's nobody like that!

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:43.060
You don't have to be so stubborn about it.

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:49.070
What is your girlfriend's name?

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.820
Hana. Hana Sugurono.

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:58.910
Semimaru, do you have any experience
living out in the wild?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.000
Not really.
I've been a city boy my whole life.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.040
I see.

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:06.960
Say, have you seen or heard any birds
since we landed on this island?

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:08.130
What?

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:09.510
How about any reptiles?

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:12.090
This island is way too quiet.

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:14.300
Do you think that's normal?

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:17.140
If it isn't normal,
then what is this place?

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.640
You must know something, Big Sis!

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.980
The atmosphere is heavy.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.110
Yes.

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:29.030
Let's get through here quickly
and head over there.

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:32.490
We should get a better view
of our surroundings from up there.

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:33.620
Right.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:37.950
What is this?

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:39.540
A pitcher plant!

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:40.960
It's a carnivorous species!

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:43.040
If I fell in...

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:44.210
You would be eaten!

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:46.420
Are you okay?

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:49.170
Yes. Thanks for saving me.

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:51.300
This thing is dangerous.
Let's get away from it.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:52.510
Right.

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:55.640
You know...

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:57.010
Does that seem normal?

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.220
What?

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:00.230
Do they even grow that big?

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:04.600
In fact, are we even in Japan?

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:07.980
-Arashi!
-I'm okay! I'll just...

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:10.490
Give me the knife!

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:11.440
Right!

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:13.950
The knife...

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:16.530
Ms. Iwashimizu! Shit!

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.410
What the hell are these?

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:21.910
-Semimaru!
-Right!

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:27.920
-Dear God in Heaven...
-No! Get off me!

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.880
have we truly arrived?

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:32.800
-I'm going to have to get serious.
-A little help, Sis!

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:36.220
Arashi?

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.310
Thank you very much.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.020
Thank god.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:49.820
You must be a member
of the rescue party, right?

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:53.240
No, I'm like you guys.

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:54.490
What?

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.540
This is unlike any place
you've ever known.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.290
You need to have a knife on you
at all times.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:09.040
Well, do you know why we're here?

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:13.170
Oh, in fact, who are you?

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:18.050
So, who the hell are you, really?

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:20.560
I used to be
a run-of-the-mill police officer.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:21.470
What?

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:24.600
I'm sorry! I won't ever do it again!
I promise!

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:26.060
What are you talking about?

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:28.520
Anyway, I'm more worried about those two.

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:31.440
However, before that...

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:34.990
You should avoid eating the intestines.

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:36.780
They live off poisonous plants.

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:37.740
Okay.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:44.330
Please tell us what you know.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:48.000
When we woke up,
we were adrift on the ocean.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:52.500
This meat is pretty good!

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:53.920
It's a bit tough, though.

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:57.300
I've never seen anyone handle a knife
the way you do, Big Sis!

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:58.510
Is that so?

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:02.010
My mother never cooked a thing.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:05.140
Oh, I should mention
that I didn't have a dad.

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:08.020
My mom was always hooking up
with different guys.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:10.770
I was just extra baggage to her.

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:15.150
One time, when she was drunk,
she said something crazy to me.

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:16.950
"Hey, Semimaru.

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:20.700
I sold you to the government
for a hundred million yen."

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:25.160
Maybe you can tell me
what she actually meant by that, Big Sis.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:32.380
You weren't kidnapped.

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:34.500
This is part of a government project.

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:36.380
You haven't heard yet?

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:41.090
What do you mean? What project?

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:43.890
So, this is where you were.

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:46.310
Who are you?

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:47.600
I'm Mozu.

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.810
I got separated from
the other members of the group.

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:53.820
Let me guess. You two were planning
to run off, weren't you?

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:57.320
Looks like these two
also had their doubts about you, Big Sis.

00:10:57.400 --> 00:11:00.780
I guess that's no surprise.
You sure do seem suspicious.

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:03.950
Fine, I'll explain myself.

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:08.330
The truth is that we're still missing
some members of the group.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:10.540
There were supposed to be seven in total.

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:13.000
Not including myself, your guide.

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:16.840
I wanted to wait
until everyone was together, but...

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.170
I'll explain everything now.

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:22.510
You may find it difficult to believe,
but just hear me out.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:27.470
There was a scientist who predicted
that a meteorite would strike the Earth.

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:30.640
That's one of those
Armageddon prophecies, right?

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:34.310
No, not at all.
It was a calculated prediction.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:38.610
A scientist accurately predicted it
from solid data.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:42.820
And not just one, but many others
in multiple countries around the world.

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:45.700
<i>Dozens of kilometers in diameter,</i>

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:49.000
<i>the meteorite's impact would cause</i>

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:54.250
<i>enormous earthquakes, volcanic eruptions,
and giant tsunamis.</i>

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:58.590
<i>On top of that, the dust would
encompass the entire Earth.</i>

00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:03.010
<i>Without sunlight, global temperatures
would drop ten to twenty degrees.</i>

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:06.260
Numerous measures were considered.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:09.970
Like blowing the thing up with a missile,
like in the movies?

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:11.390
That was one option.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:12.440
Seriously?

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:15.610
I'm telling you, this is serious!
I'm not joking!

00:12:17.650 --> 00:12:23.030
After all the measures were explored,
they worked out a worst-case scenario.

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:27.530
If humanity was wiped out, they designed
a way to ensure we wouldn't go extinct.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:30.450
It was known as the 7SEEDS Project.

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:38.380
<i>They would select young, healthy people
and put them in cryosleep.</i>

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:43.050
<i>While the Earth faced a cataclysm,
they would sleep.</i>

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:46.050
<i>When it was determined
that the Earth was once again inhabitable,</i>

00:12:46.340 --> 00:12:48.350
<i>they would be defrosted and released.</i>

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:52.430
Just like a seed that survives the winter
to be planted in the spring.

00:12:53.180 --> 00:12:55.400
Hence the name 7SEEDS.

00:12:55.850 --> 00:12:57.900
You are now the seeds of humanity.

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:04.740
I am your guide.

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:08.410
I'm here to tell you the truth
and provide support.

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:10.740
So, you underwent survival training?

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:11.700
Yes.

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:13.120
No wonder you...

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:15.040
Wait just a damn minute!

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:16.460
If that's all true,

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:20.380
us and the other three
are the only people left on Earth?

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:23.130
No, the project was carried out
by every country.

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:25.930
In Japan, five teams were made.

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:28.590
Teams Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter.

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:31.640
Summer was split into teams A and B.

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:34.100
We are Team Summer B.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:38.230
The members of each team were selected

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:40.230
according to certain factors
by a computer.

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:45.400
Without being told, you were taken away
one night in your sleep

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:46.950
to be put into cryosleep.

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:49.910
So, that's what she meant
about the hundred million yen.

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:52.450
You're lying!
Why wouldn't they give us a choice?

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:56.000
That doesn't make any sense!
I refuse to accept it!

00:13:57.620 --> 00:14:01.380
It's too late to fuss over
whether you agreed to it or not.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:02.630
Shut up!

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:05.720
Face the facts.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:07.720
There's no way.

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:09.510
Hana...

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:12.930
Will I never see you again?

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:16.060
This is bullshit!

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:17.520
Arashi!

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:29.490
Arashi...

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:36.120
If what she said just now is really true,
how much time has actually passed?

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:39.870
Ten years? Twenty? Maybe even a hundred?

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:41.330
Maybe more?

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:44.750
No. I...

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.720
I won't believe it.
I don’t want to believe it!

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:57.730
No sign of the bugs.

00:14:57.810 --> 00:14:58.640
Yes.

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:01.810
Is something wrong, Hana?

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:04.070
I smell something strange
coming from Mr. Yanagi.

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:08.400
That smell...

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:11.280
Mr. Yanagi, I want to ask you something.

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:12.530
What is it?

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:16.080
This "project" that you talked about,

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:18.790
I understand we didn't have a choice,

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:21.960
but why did you agree to take part
as our leader?

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:24.340
Is that what you want to know?

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:30.300
I've always had a passion for war films
and I've always admired war heroes.

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:37.770
That's why I decided to join the JSDF,
but we never saw any war.

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:40.180
Hell, we didn't even get
to fire a damn gun.

00:15:40.770 --> 00:15:46.320
As you know, this place is filled
with danger, and threats are everywhere.

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:50.150
I came here to protect
women and children...

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:52.700
Are you okay?

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:54.660
Yes.

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:59.450
Anyway, what I want right now is...

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:02.420
Mr. Yanagi?

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:08.050
This is the place, just in here.

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:10.590
-What?
-You want us to go inside?

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:13.930
The key to our survival is in here.

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.930
You want to keep on living, right?

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:19.970
You don't want those bugs
to kill you, right?

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:23.100
Then, follow me.

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:30.780
This smell...

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:32.780
I'm scared!

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:33.990
It's all right.

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:35.780
It's dark in here.

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:47.130
Daddy, is that wasp trying to eat
the dead caterpillar?

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:48.880
Not quite, Hana.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:51.510
The caterpillar is just paralyzed.

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:54.010
The wasp is laying its eggs inside of it.

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:58.300
When the babies hatch, they'll grow
by feeding on the living caterpillar.

00:16:58.390 --> 00:17:01.810
So, it ends up getting eaten alive.

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:03.560
This is not good.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:04.690
Hana?

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:06.310
We shouldn't be here!

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:08.060
Stop!

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:11.650
Mr. Yanagi, there is no key
to our survival in here, is there?

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:13.950
You're just luring us into a trap, right?

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:19.780
Hey, old man!

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:25.250
Holy shit!

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:34.760
We're screwed!

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:36.470
We'll be larva food, too?

00:17:37.590 --> 00:17:41.560
I wanted to be a doctor
and become an astronaut.

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:44.600
Haru! Stop freaking out
and follow my lead!

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:50.190
This flame isn't enough.

00:17:50.770 --> 00:17:53.650
Old man! Didn't you just tell us
you admired heroes?

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:55.570
Going out like this makes you a villain!

00:17:55.650 --> 00:17:56.530
Mr. Yanagi!

00:17:56.610 --> 00:17:57.780
Please save us!

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:02.200
Mr. Yanagi!

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:06.000
If we all die here,
then the project will be a huge failure!

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:09.630
Do you really want it to end like this?

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:17.880
Get ready to run.

00:18:18.470 --> 00:18:23.220
Team Spring was put into cryosleep
under Tokyo.

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:28.520
That means we're near
the shores of the Kanto region.

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:33.150
If you go west,
you should eventually find land.

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:37.320
Mr. Yanagi!

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:45.370
Search for the seven Fujis.

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:50.120
There, you will find the means to survive.

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:51.670
Let's run while we have a chance!

00:18:52.460 --> 00:18:53.420
Hana!

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:55.550
Right.

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:03.760
<i>I wasn't able...</i>

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:08.810
<i>to be a hero...</i>

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:12.810
<i>But I want you all to live.</i>

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:26.040
The old man was serious about this.
He came here prepared to die.

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:28.870
I could never do that.

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:32.120
I wonder if the guides
of the other teams are the same way?

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:34.630
Hana?

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:37.380
Ultimately, he saved us.

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:39.630
All of us.

00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:47.810
He said something about searching for
the seven Fujis, right?

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:51.100
Starting from the north,
I think that's Mt. Akan Fuji,

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:56.320
Mt. Natori Fuji, Mt. Noto Fuji,
Mt. Ogino Fuji, Mt. Fuji, Mt. Kobe Fuji,

00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:58.940
Mt. Tosa Fuji, and Mt. Bungo Fuji.

00:19:59.030 --> 00:20:01.240
He said we were in the Kanto region.

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:02.740
Which one of those is the closest?

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:04.160
Mt. Ogino Fuji.

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:05.660
Okay, then that's our destination.

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:08.080
For now, let's make a new raft.

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:10.450
Wow. You sure are optimistic, Tsunomata.

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:11.580
Well, like they say,

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:14.170
"Rich or poor,
we all end up in the same place."

00:20:14.540 --> 00:20:16.250
Thinking of it that way
helps me keep going.

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:17.960
Oh, I've heard that before!

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:20.970
So, where do we end up?
Some promised land?

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:22.430
No, not a promised land.

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:24.260
It means we end up six feet under.

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:25.970
Hey, everybody.

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:29.520
You might not have an appetite now,
but I'll start making something.

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:32.480
Thanks. You're amazing, Chisa.

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:33.440
What?

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:36.020
My father always used to tell me,

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:39.860
"People who remember the necessities,
even at the worst of times,

00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:41.360
are the strongest among us."

00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:44.320
No, I just like eating.

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:45.910
I'll eat, too!

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:50.160
Where did Haru go?

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:56.380
What are you doing?

00:20:57.330 --> 00:20:58.380
<i>Hana,</i>

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:00.710
what do you think is
the easiest way to die?

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:03.470
What are you talking about?

00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:06.890
Mr. Yanagi just saved your life,
didn't he?

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:09.180
And he gave us the goal
of going to Mt. Ogino Fuji.

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:10.310
That wasn't my goal.

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:13.560
My goal was the piano competition
at the end of the year.

00:21:14.690 --> 00:21:17.440
It was my last chance
to go to an international competition.

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:20.230
Who decided it was your last chance?

00:21:20.650 --> 00:21:23.110
That's something we decide for ourselves.

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:26.450
We keep going as long as we don't give up!

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:28.070
Things don't just end.

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:32.580
If we keep pushing on,
there's no such thing as the end!

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:37.080
Why are you the one crying, Hana?

00:21:38.420 --> 00:21:41.750
You're telling me that, but I think you're
the one who really needed to hear it.

00:21:42.340 --> 00:21:43.840
You sure are selfish.

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:45.170
Shut it.

00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:47.930
I just wanted to try saying that line.

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:50.390
I never actually want to experience
what it's like to drown.

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:51.850
Why all the theatrics?

00:21:51.930 --> 00:21:53.890
-Haru!
-Hana!

00:21:53.970 --> 00:21:55.430
Hey! Come on!

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:56.640
Let's head back.

00:21:58.190 --> 00:21:59.810
<i>I'm not giving up.</i>

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:03.070
<i>So don't you dare give up either, Arashi.</i>

00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:06.740
Are those all the supplies?
It's time to go.

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:09.910
I just hope the weather holds up
this time.

00:22:13.740 --> 00:22:16.790
It's okay. I don't smell any rain.
